From a6b9a92ca7921e62b8bdce0a0b6ea4e5fa3e590a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:54:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI search first, a click searches the map, the hovered home
 in brass, and no 'back soon' on a CRM hiccup

- The search box is an AI search, labelled so, on its own row: 'Tell me everything
  you want and why. I'll find you houses.' The AI reads the whole sentence, the
  goal behind it as well as the features, and says in one line what it understood.
  It never filters on who a person is. The filters follow, price first, with
  restyled dropdowns. On a phone the box wraps to two lines and keeps its button.
- Moving or zooming the map no longer searches again. A click on the map searches
  around that spot, and a brass ring shows the area searched.
- A home the visitor points at, in the list or on the map, turns Chapter3 brass.
- A CRM GET that fails with a 502, 503, 504 or a network error is tried once more,
  and a signed-in listing that still fails shows the public copy instead of the
  'back soon' page.
